# Netlify redirects
# The free reactivation pilot was replaced by The First 10 (paid entry offer,
# guaranteed outcome). Anything already shared pointing at /pilot lands on the
# live offer instead of the retired page.
#
# The trailing "!" is required: without it Netlify serves the existing
# pilot.html and ignores the rule. The file is kept on disk (and in git) but is
# unreachable while these rules are in place.
/pilot        /first-10   301!
/pilot.html   /first-10   301!

# /intel is internal tooling, not site content. The publish directory is the
# repo root, so without these rules the sales playbook, the scoring priors and
# the objection handling would all be fetchable on the live domain.
#
# Note this only covers Netlify. It does NOT make the directory private on
# GitHub — the repo is public, so anything committed here is readable there
# regardless of these rules.
/intel        /404.html   404!
/intel/*      /404.html   404!
